From 0796c5dccbad1b13679ff1eedb2af5ccff84567c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:02:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0382 -- the legacy route finder's three
 output-identical levers behind a TEMPORARY switch, default OFF:
 DOSAGS_ROUTE_FAST=1 (stamp grid instead of the 0xFF fill, active-slot
 frontier walk, inline line-of-sight walk)

WHY: on the moving fixture MS3 about 60% of the skipped frames are click ticks, and a warm click tick is the legacy
route search (MMD is game data v25, so MaskRouteFinder is the legacy finder): ~85% of the tick's excess is FindRoute.
The lab split it (lab-rb docs/lab/move-lab/ms99): per call find_route_dijkstra refills beenhere with 0xFF for the whole
mask (W x H x 2 bytes), every pass rescans every trail slot, and the smoothing's can_see_from walks a whole line through
a callback after the first wall is already known.

WHAT (one switch, read once, tested once per CALL -- never inside a search loop):
- unset (default): find_route_dijkstra and do_line run as they were; their text is untouched by this patch.
- DOSAGS_ROUTE_FAST=1:
  R1  find_route_dijkstra_fast keeps a uint8 generation stamp per mask cell. A cell is unvisited when its stamp is not
      the current generation, which is what the 0xFF fill said; the only read of a possibly-unvisited cell is CHECK_MIN's
      first test. beenhere stays the per-call buffer it is. At generation 255 the grid is cleared and restarts at 1.
  R2  each pass walks a bitset of the active slots (visited != -1 and vstate != 2), kept at every write that kills or
      revives a slot: the same candidates in the same order.
  R3  can_see_from walks Allegro do_line's exact pixel sequence inline on an 8-bit mask (outside the bitmap = wall, as
      getpixel's -1), stopping at the first wall; other depths keep do_line.
- Memory: the stamp grid is W x H bytes (64,000 for a 320 x 200 mask, 192,000 for 960 x 200), one grid at a time,
  allocated at the first search on a mask size, freed and re-allocated when the size changes, freed in
  ~LegacyRouteFinder. A failed allocation quits ("insufficient memory to allocate pathfinder stamp buffer") -- a new
  failure mode only when W x H more bytes are missing; today's per-call beenhere buffer of twice that size is unchecked.
- Witness: RUNMANIFEST "DOS-PORT routefast on= stamp_allocs= stamp_peak_bytes="; DOSAGS_ROUTE_FAST joins the
  environment witness list.

EVIDENCE (lab DOSBox-X, fixed cycles; the lab's switchless build SW123 has this ON body): identical answers to the
unmodified finder on MS3's 114 route calls, a 5,292-request grid corpus and 2,892 cross-split requests over MMD, 5days
and Trilby, both flavours, at stamp ranges 255 / 1 / 2 / 3, with Dijkstra's trail-cap exit and the try_this_square
fallback exercised (RESULT-RSW-1). Lab model of the 486: MS3 571 -> 407 skips at the release level (RESULT-RSW-2);
nothing is measured on the 486 yet.

TEMPORARY: the switch exists for a same-binary 486 A/B. After that round and the operator's ruling on the default, a
following patch removes the switch and the body that lost.
